Compositing manager notes.
==========================

The compositor is built and enabled by default (--disable-compositor turns it
off at build time, "xfwm4 --compositor=off" or the /general/use_compositing
xfconf setting at run time).

Windows are drawn with OpenGL when the driver allows it and with XRender
otherwise. /general/use_gl_compositing switches between the two, and
XFWM4_GL_BACKEND=glx makes the OpenGL renderer use GLX instead of EGL.

README.md describes the OpenGL renderer, its settings, and when it falls
back to XRender.

vblank and tearing
------------------

Sync to vblank is selected with the "--vblank" command line option or the
/general/vblank_mode xfconf setting, read at startup only:

  $ xfwm4 --replace --vblank=auto &
  $ xfconf-query -c xfwm4 -p /general/vblank_mode -s auto

  auto      sync every frame to the screen (default)
  adaptive  stop syncing when the frame rate falls below the refresh rate;
            needs GLX (XFWM4_GL_BACKEND=glx) or XRender and
            GLX_EXT_swap_control_tear, otherwise same as auto
  off       no sync

  glx       XRender only: sync through GLX (libepoxy at build time)
  xpresent  XRender only: sync through the Present extension (libXpresent at
            build time)

With the OpenGL renderer, "glx" and "xpresent" behave like "auto".

"xfwm4 --version" lists which of these were enabled at build time.
